[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   TEP-9 step 099 -- Heliospheric geometry and probe/ISO asymptotes
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Scores the TEP boundary axis (49 deg, -17 deg ecliptic) and its
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   60-deg caps against the measured geometry of the heliospheric
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   interface and of every object that has physically crossed -- or is
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   crossing -- the relevant boundary sector:
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Reference directions (literature anchors, cited):
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   * ISM inflow (upwind)          (255.8, +5.16)
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   * heliotail apex (downwind)    ( 75.8, -5.16)
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   * IBEX ribbon centre           (221.0, +39.0)
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   * pristine ISMF direction      (227.28, +34.62)  Zirnstein+16
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Escaping spacecraft (heliocentric velocity asymptote at epoch
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   2026-01-01, JPL Horizons vector ephemeris):
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Voyager 1 (-31), Voyager 2 (-32), Pioneer 10 (-23),
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Pioneer 11 (-24), New Horizons (-98)
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Interstellar objects (inbound velocity asymptote from SBDB
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   hyperbolic elements):
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   1I/'Oumuamua, 2I/Borisov, 3I/ATLAS
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   Tests
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   1. Separations: every direction vs the axis and anti-axis; cap
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   membership at the 60-deg radius used throughout the paper.
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   2. Axis-vs-heliosphere proximity: angular distance from the axis to
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   the ISM-inflow antipode (heliotail apex) and to the ISMF
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   direction, with a uniform-direction p-value for each.
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   3. Probe alibi: how many escaping-probe asymptotes fall inside the
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   cap vs the mirror cap -- the geometric fact behind "why has no
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   spacecraft seen the boundary directly".  Reported descriptively
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   (probe directions are not a random draw).
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   4. ISO arrivals: inbound asymptotes vs caps; a dated datum for the
[2026-09-21 15:11:08 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 099]   ISO-arrival channel.
